# The repo root .gitignore blanket-excludes *.skp (no user/client binary
# models committed) but only allowlists a few specific fixture directories
# per package - re-include this package's own two exceptions, both
# disclosed plainly in create.dart's own module doc comment:
#
# - lib/src/scaffold/blank_v17.skp: the bundled blank-document scaffold
#   openskp.create splices new geometry into (SketchUp SDK's own built-in
#   empty-document boilerplate, not user/client data - same file, same
#   disclosure, as packages/python/src/openskp/_scaffold/blank_v17.skp,
#   already allowlisted there).
# - test/fixtures/create_reference/*.skp: deterministic reference files
#   this package's own create_test.dart byte-compares its output against,
#   generated once by the real, SDK-validated Python writer (not user
#   data either - synthetic test geometry only). The root .gitignore's own
#   `!packages/dart/test/fixtures/*.skp` allow doesn't reach this nested
#   subdirectory.
!lib/src/scaffold/*.skp
!test/fixtures/create_reference/*.skp
